{"t": 1794105635.5105438, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502s \u2014 root cause found and fixed in code.\n\nCause: CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api` shows `export_rows()` failing with `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` (4,120 occurrences). Upstream ledger 2026.11 added `currency` to every row, but the CSV exporter only allowed `id`/`amount`, so every export request raised.\n\nFix: added `currency` to the DictWriter fieldnames in `reports/export.py`. Tested with rows that include and omit `currency` (missing values export as empty). Needs a deploy, then re-run the failed exports."}, "ok": true}
